## [2.1.20260904162413] - 2026-09-04 16:24:13

### ADD

- Added **ALPN** field support: Node links now automatically include ALPN parameters, adapting to more client scenarios.

### Debug

- Fixed **HTTPS Proxy**: Handshake failure when upstream server requests client certificate (CertificateRequest); now replies with an empty certificate to properly complete the handshake. [Commit](https://github.com/cmliu/CF-Workers-CheckSocks5/commit/ae93bc28462a6df03795143a5caa85f717ba231a)

## [2.1.20260811144522] - 2026-08-11 14:45:22

### Change

- Optimized **XHTTP** upstream transmission: Added data packet batching mechanism. Small chunks of data are merged before being sent together, reducing frequent small packet writes, lowering resource overhead, and making large file uploads smoother.

## [2.1.20260810030901] - 2026-08-10 03:09:01

### ADD

- Added **XHTTP obfs padding** receiver support: Recognizes `xPaddingObfsMode` (tokenish / queryInHeader) obfuscation headers.

## [2.1.20260809231057] - 2026-08-09 23:10:57

### Debug

- Fixed **XHTTP chained proxy** parameter parsing: Trailing slash in path caused reverse proxy configurations to fail; now supports trailing slashes.

## [2.1.20260809201158] - 2026-08-09 20:11:58

### Change

- Optimized **XHTTP** transmission pipeline: TCP data is now bi-directionally piped using `request.body.pipeTo(socket.writable)` and `socket.readable.pipeTo(IdentityTransformStream)` directly, bypassing ReadableStream + upstream write queue + BYOB/Grain chunk copying, significantly reducing CPU usage.
- Optimized **XHTTP** connection management: `forwardataTCP` added a "connect-only" mode that establishes connection and writes the initial packet, then directly returns socket for pipe pass-through, while preserving the fallback logic to automatically switch to reverse proxy upon direct connection failure (gRPC/WS callers unaffected).
- Optimized **XHTTP UDP** handling: UDP branch separated into dedicated handler function, maintaining Trojan UDP reverse proxy and DNS forwarding logic.

## [2.1.20260729235734] - 2026-07-29 23:57:34

### Change

- Corrected **PRELOAD_RACE_DIAL** environment variable logic: Default value changed from `true` to `false` (disabled by default); setting `1` or `true` enables it; updated README description accordingly. [Commit](https://github.com/cmliu/edgetunnel/commit/aea8b85688ef6066116af551cfd5e6fd2ce77567)

## [2.1.20260724150359] - 2026-07-24 15:03:59

### Change

- Synchronized latest **GrainTCP** transmission optimizations: Upstream Grain batching target adjusted from `16KB` to `20KB`, reusing unified buffering/batching core; sequential small chunks opportunistically merge during drain phase, reducing frequent `writer.write()` calls. [Upstream Commit](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP/commit/1d22628f4d1413989f521f1d41591b0c72e658eb)
- Optimized downstream **GrainTCP** aggregation: Maintained `32KB` aggregation limit, using `tail * 12` low water mark and up to 4 rounds of 1ms growth observation; flush can send multiple aggregated packets consecutively when near limit, reducing small WebSocket frame count. [Upstream Commit](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP/commit/1d22628f4d1413989f521f1d41591b0c72e658eb)
- Optimized downstream packet processing: Large chunks sent directly when Grain is empty; small chunks detached from reusable read buffer in BYOB/default reader path first; aggregated results copied before sending to avoid scratch buffer overwrites. [Upstream Commit](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP/commit/1d22628f4d1413989f521f1d41591b0c72e658eb)
- Enhanced TCP connection management based on upstream model: Added connection generation, socket identity, and old downstream drain barrier; upstream data continues buffering and waits for new writer during redialing, preventing asynchronous cleanup from polluting new connections. [Upstream Concept](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP/commit/1d22628f4d1413989f521f1d41591b0c72e658eb)
- Unified direct send, chunked send, and periodic flush serial sending chain based on upstream Grain sending model, persisting async send errors; response headers consumed only on first real send, avoiding premature consumption on redial or invalid connections. [Upstream Concept](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP/commit/1d22628f4d1413989f521f1d41591b0c72e658eb)
- Maintained multi-protocol compatibility: WS upstream uses non-blocking enqueue to reduce message processing delay; XHTTP/gRPC continues waiting for remote write completion; retained local `16MiB / 4096` entry high water mark protection to prevent unbounded Worker queue growth. [Upstream Change](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP/commit/1d22628f4d1413989f521f1d41591b0c72e658eb)
- Optimized local speed test response to trigger only in **reverse proxy mode**; speed test requests are forwarded normally when using **SOCKS5/HTTP/HTTPS/TURN/SSTP** proxy.

## [2.1.20260722191426] - 2026-07-22 19:14:26

